  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9266273b8f123004195741f969177dda, type: 3}
  title: Standalone Systems
  sections:
  - heading: What are standalone systems ?
    text: They are toolkits that don't need anything else from the project to work.
      The project depends on them, but they don't depend on the project.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Assembly definitions
    text: Each standalone system should have it's own assembly definition, to make
      sure that it does not inadvertently use a Cooking Carnage type.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
